+## Grasp beyond the top-down envelope: tilted orientation search, then a table relay
+
+**Trigger.** yam_real: solve_ik(backend='mink') of the top-down grasp fails ('best configuration is 0.03-0.16 m from the target') because the object is far from the shoulders, while the place step needs a vertical approach. Search pitch 90->30 deg and yaw 0/+-30 deg with an 8 cm stand-off along the approach axis. Gripper empty while searching. Cost: 2 IK calls per orientation (~0.02 s each, no ticks). If the result is not top-down, set the object down at a relay point that the inserting arm reaches top-down (search a grid around the midpoint of the two arms' home EE positions, at least 8 cm clear of other objects). Then park the arm, re-localize, and re-grasp top-down.
+
+```python
+def qmul(a, b):
+    return (a[0]*b[0]-a[1]*b[1]-a[2]*b[2]-a[3]*b[3], a[0]*b[1]+a[1]*b[0]+a[2]*b[3]-a[3]*b[2],
+            a[0]*b[2]-a[1]*b[3]+a[2]*b[0]+a[3]*b[1], a[0]*b[3]+a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1]+a[3]*b[0])
+
+home_q = {a: tuple(float(v) for v in get_robot_state().end_effector_poses[a].quaternion_wxyz) for a in ("left", "right")}
+
+def tool_quat(arm, pitch_deg, yaw_deg):   # home tool points +x; pitch 90 = straight down
+    p = math.radians(pitch_deg) / 2.0
+    y = math.radians(yaw_deg) / 2.0
+    return qmul((math.cos(y), 0.0, 0.0, math.sin(y)), qmul((math.cos(p), 0.0, math.sin(p), 0.0), home_q[arm]))
+
+def approach_dir(q):   # tool z axis in world
+    w, x, y, z = q
+    return (2 * (x * z + w * y), 2 * (y * z - w * x), 1 - 2 * (x * x + y * y))
+
+def grasp_plan(arm, gx, gy, gz, stand_off=0.08):
+    for pitch, yaw in [(90, 0)] + [(p, y) for p in (75, 60, 45, 30) for y in (0, 30, -30)]:
+        q = tool_quat(arm, pitch, yaw)
+        a = approach_dir(q)
+        pre = (gx - stand_off * a[0], gy - stand_off * a[1], gz - stand_off * a[2])
+        if solve_ik(Pose((gx, gy, gz), q, get_robot_state().base_frame), arm=arm, backend="mink").ok and \
+           solve_ik(Pose(pre, q, get_robot_state().base_frame), arm=arm, backend="mink").ok:
+            return {"q": q, "pre": pre, "grasp": (gx, gy, gz), "pitch": pitch}
+    return None
+```
+
+**Evidence.** dev seeds 51, 53, 54, 55 (gear out of top-down reach; picked at pitch 45-75 deg) and unseen-check 67, 68, 69 all passed through the relay; v00 (top-down only) 0/5
+
+*Provenance:* yam_real/gear_assembly/task_0 (yamlab Isaac Sim bridge, station yam-isaac), campaign 2026-10-19_14-32-22_gear-isaac; dev 51-55, held-out 3/10 for the whole program (fix_code.py v05). Verified 5/5 on dev seeds by an independent verifier (2026-10-19).
+
+*Verifier gaps:* does not say which arm picks vs inserts on a two-arm station (seed 51 became a left-pick / right-insert handoff); gives no lift move after a tilted grasp (the vertical lift returned PLANNER_FAILED on 2/3 tilted picks, harmlessly); the relay grid spacing and the picking arm's IK check at the relay are implicit. **Limit:** this reaches the *pick*; it does not extend a top-down *insertion*. On yam-isaac every seed whose target shaft was >= ~0.485 m from the right arm base failed with no top-down IK at the insert pose (held-out 3, 5, 7, 8, 9; unseen 66).
