+## Top-down grasp of a hubbed gear: hub-top centre, 10 mm deep
+
+**Trigger.** Gear (or any part with a raised hub over a wider flange) lying flat, seen from the metric camera 'top', to be grasped top-down on yam_real. Prompt 'light blue gear' (the flat gear base also answers, so bound the projected extent at both ends). Measured on yam-isaac: hub top is the highest 2% of the cloud, teeth top 22.5 mm lower (radial z-profile from the hub centre). The jaw contacts at least 6.5 mm below the EE point, so a 16 mm depth closed on the teeth. Gripper empty on approach; one move_to_pose per segment (~3.7 s wall).
+
+```python
+seg = segment_text("top", "light blue gear")
+best = None
+for cand in seg.segmentations[:8]:
+    cloud = mask_to_point_cloud(cand, "top", target_frame=get_robot_state().base_frame)
+    xs = sorted(float(p[0]) for p in cloud.points)
+    ys = sorted(float(p[1]) for p in cloud.points)
+    if len(xs) < 30:
+        continue
+    ext_x = xs[int(0.95 * (len(xs) - 1))] - xs[int(0.05 * (len(xs) - 1))]
+    ext_y = ys[int(0.95 * (len(ys) - 1))] - ys[int(0.05 * (len(ys) - 1))]
+    if 0.015 < ext_x < 0.07 and 0.015 < ext_y < 0.07 and (best is None or cand.score > best[0]):
+        best = (float(cand.score), cloud)   # bounded both ends: the 20 cm gear base also answers this prompt
+if best is None:
+    raise ValueError("gear not found")
+zs = sorted(float(p[2]) for p in best[1].points)
+hub_top = zs[int(0.98 * (len(zs) - 1))]
+top = [p for p in best[1].points if float(p[2]) > hub_top - 0.004]
+gear_x = sum(float(p[0]) for p in top) / len(top)    # centre of the hub's top face
+gear_y = sum(float(p[1]) for p in top) / len(top)
+HUB_GRASP_DEPTH = 0.010   # TCP below the hub top; 0.016 closed on the teeth 22.5 mm below the top
+grasp_z = hub_top - HUB_GRASP_DEPTH
+```
+
+**Evidence.** v03 (16 mm): seed 52 failed (jaw width 0.66, gear jammed tilted). v04/v05 (10 mm): 5/5 dev, widths 0.41-0.52
+
+*Provenance:* yam_real/gear_assembly/task_0 (yamlab Isaac Sim bridge, station yam-isaac), campaign 2026-10-19_14-32-22_gear-isaac; dev 51-55, held-out 3/10 for the whole program (fix_code.py v05). Verified 5/5 on dev seeds by an independent verifier (2026-10-19).
+
+*Verifier gap:* no entry gives the seat height for an insertion. The verifier derived EE z = plate surface_z + (grasp_z - table_z), segmenting the table ('wooden table') for table_z. On held-out seeds 1 and 2 the insertion stalled ~15 mm above the seat with the TCP 4-6 mm off the shaft axis and there is no recovery; treat insertion as unsolved.
